Private party auto loans are a type of secured loan, using the vehicle as collateral. If the seller still owes money on the car, your lender may need to pay off the seller's lender first. Then, your lender will give the remaining amount to the seller. Doing it this way ensures that you're getting the car with a clear title. 

As with other types of auto loans, you will need to meet the lender's requirements in order to be approved for financing. That can include a certain minimum credit score, proof of an adequate income, and a good credit history. For instance, if you have a negative mark on your credit report like a bankruptcy or loans going to collections, you are likely to have a harder time getting a loan than someone who doesn't.
